      "created_at": "2012-07-08T15:57:57.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;McBehrer&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"McBehrer\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>also, Plague Rat deals all hero targets 1 irreducible melee damage per turn, so he IS hitting everyone.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Exactly - thematically, we could look at the infections as coming up over multiple exposures to Plauge Rat’s attacks, not necessarily because of the specific actions of the card that brought it out. That explains why we can also play an Infection card on its own.</p>",
